 "preferred_name": "General anaesthesia",
 "kind": "skill",
 "definition": "Giving and managing drugs that put a patient into a reversible, unconscious state with no sensation, so that surgery can be done.",
 "description": {
  "text": "Medically induced loss of consciousness that leaves a patient unarousable even by painful stimuli, achieved with injected or inhaled medications, often with an analgesic and a neuromuscular blocking agent. It lets surgery be done that would otherwise be intolerably painful.",
